WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:05.650
Film Courage: three to five common mistakes
you see new actors making on set?

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:16.650
Bill Duke, actor/filmmaker/author: Common
mistakes?

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:20.140
Number One.

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:29.619
No actors (for the most part and some actors
which it’s just that there is ego is out

00:00:29.619 --> 00:00:40.530
of shape) believe that acting is about talking
or speaking their lines.

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:46.460
They have no understanding of the art of listening.

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:48.260
We are having a conversation.

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:54.820
What a conversation is, you speak.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:01:06.500
I listen closely to what you’re saying because
I want to respond to your question.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:16.530
Most actors have memorized their line so no
matter how you say it or what’s anything,

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:21.710
they respond with their line.

00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:27.759
On camera it looks like now what a minute,
she was crying?

00:01:27.759 --> 00:01:30.490
“Oh Becky, want to go to the prom?”

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:37.429
No, no, no…she was crying when you gave
her the flower?

00:01:37.429 --> 00:01:38.770
“Oh yeah.

00:01:38.770 --> 00:01:40.109
Take two.”

00:01:40.109 --> 00:01:43.719
“Hey Becky, want to go to the promo?”

00:01:43.719 --> 00:01:45.349
[Laughs]

00:01:45.349 --> 00:01:46.979
“Cut!”

00:01:46.979 --> 00:01:57.380
We’re going to have a long talk in the corner,
okay?

00:01:57.380 --> 00:02:10.619
Second biggest mistake I think is that 
some actors are not collaborators.

00:02:10.619 --> 00:02:19.700
You know it’s like they’re so insecure,
it’s their scene.

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:23.880
And so they go in with the attitude like “Well,
this is my scene because I have more lines

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:24.880
than you.”

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:32.340
And there’s two people on the scene, there’s
two people on the scene.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:37.159
You are doing a monologue if it’s just you.

00:02:37.159 --> 00:02:42.560
But there are people’s egos that are just
so large that you’re not even there.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:51.579
So it’s like that’s how good they can
be and that’s annoying as hell.

00:02:51.579 --> 00:02:59.750
The third thing is nerves.

00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:12.859
I mean I’ve literally seen…I’ve had
to stop shooting a scene because in the middle

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:21.200
of the scene the actor was sweating so badly
that we had to cut.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.709
“Are you okay?”

00:03:22.709 --> 00:03:24.280
“What happened?

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:25.849
What happened?”

00:03:25.849 --> 00:03:33.170
When I say sweat, I’m talking about [motions
all down the face] because internally they

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:37.909
are so worried about the fact that they are
not doing it right that they just…something

00:03:37.909 --> 00:03:43.260
internally happens and they are just terrified.

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:50.510
So as a director you get a call and you give
them…make sure that they know they are protected.

00:03:50.510 --> 00:04:01.029
You’ve got to give them assurance because
acting is responding, it’s surrendering.

00:04:01.029 --> 00:04:04.769
It’s not holding on to safety.

00:04:04.769 --> 00:04:10.800
That’s easy for me to say but try it sometimes.

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:15.129
Try going in and trying to do it and you don’t
know how it’s going to turn out.

00:04:15.129 --> 00:04:16.129
You ask

00:04:16.129 --> 00:04:17.129
“How is it?

00:04:17.129 --> 00:04:18.389
How did it go?”

00:04:18.389 --> 00:04:20.970
“It was great.”

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:22.240
“Can I see it?”

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:28.650
You don’t know how it was because you were
involved in it and not knowing what to do

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:34.530
is…we’re not feeling safe that you’ve
done it well.

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:37.240
It’s a challenge.

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:43.830
Film Courage: Well, they say having a big
ego and a small ego is pretty much the same

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:47.590
thing, it’s just sort of different ways
of dealing with it?

00:04:47.590 --> 00:05:01.720
Bill Duke: Having a big ego I think is a sign
of small self-regard.

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:07.270
Having a small ego is similar.

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:18.430
I think…I forgot his name but Wayne Dyer
(I love Wayne Dyer)?

00:05:18.430 --> 00:05:32.030
He said “The key to having a great life
is to get rid of your ego.”

00:05:32.030 --> 00:05:35.000
And the audience said “What are you talking
about?”

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:39.330
He said “Do you know what the word ego stands
for?

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:40.330
E.G.O.”

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:47.680
He goes to the board and says “E. Edging.

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:49.789
G. God.

00:05:49.789 --> 00:05:53.430
O. Out.”

00:05:53.430 --> 00:06:02.220
He said “Your ego edges God out.

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:10.340
And without that force in your life you have
nothing but empty accomplishments.”

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:21.449
And he says “Try eating those empty accomplishments
when you’re sitting home alone because nobody

00:06:21.449 --> 00:06:24.140
likes you in your mansion.”

00:06:24.140 --> 00:06:29.970
He said “It’s more comfortable than being
on the street.

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:39.159
But when you ride by that person sitting on
the street, he looks familiar.”

00:06:39.159 --> 00:06:43.890
I think he’s brilliant and true.

00:06:43.890 --> 00:06:49.730
I know very wealthy people who are miserable.

00:06:49.730 --> 00:06:53.330
There are many.

00:06:53.330 --> 00:06:58.729
Money didn’t fill the hole.

00:06:58.729 --> 00:07:00.500
Cars didn’t fill the hole.

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:01.879
Clothes didn’t fill the hole.

00:07:01.879 --> 00:07:03.370
Vacations didn’t fill the hole.

00:07:03.370 --> 00:07:07.370
Relationships didn’t fill the hole.

00:07:07.370 --> 00:07:11.639
There is something else you have to have.

00:07:11.639 --> 00:07:13.910
I’m not saying I know everything.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:20.069
But I do know because I’ve had a lot of
it, that all those things don’t fill the

00:07:20.069 --> 00:07:21.069
hole.

00:07:21.069 --> 00:07:36.730
If you don’t have self-love…even if somebody
else loves you, if you don’t have self-love.

00:07:36.730 --> 00:07:47.740
I tell my daughter everyday you know, never
forget men treat you the way they see you

00:07:47.740 --> 00:07:52.380
treat yourself.

00:07:52.380 --> 00:08:04.290
Don’t treat yourself the way you think he
should perceive you.

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:11.009
Treat yourself the way you want to be treated.

00:08:11.009 --> 00:08:16.639
I think it’s a general for people, I love
quotes so…I can give you three of my favorite

00:08:16.639 --> 00:08:17.639
quotes?

00:08:17.639 --> 00:08:18.509
Film Courage: That’s sounds great.

